       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,600 mg/day of ibuprofen is three times the maximum daily dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. At that dose, the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events is high, and it doesn't give more benefit, because the anti-inflammatory and analgesic effects plateau well below it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 600 mg PO four times daily or 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day), or up to 3,200 mg/day if needed. Give me the dose and frequency, and I'll enter it.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If you're trying to get stronger pain control or anti-inflammatory effect than ibuprofen gives at its maximum dose, I can enter an adjunct or alternative agent that you choose.\n- **Take it to pharmacy.** If you think this dose is clinically justified, for example in a protocol I don't know about, you'll need to go through the pharmacy or the appropriate override process. I can add a note for the pharmacist, but I can't enter the order myself."
      }
